        <div class="col-lg-8 col-md-8 col-sm-8 col-xs-12 content">
            <article>
                <div class="tn-pagetitle show" aria-hidden="false">
    <h1>Solid Waste Program</h1>
    

</div>

                <div>




    
    
    <div class="tn-cta parbase">
    <a href="/environment/program-areas/solid-waste.html" class="text-button icon-right-1" alt="Waste Management Branch Main Page">Waste Management Branch Main Page</a>


</div>


    
    
    <div class="tn-rte">
    
        <p>The Solid Waste Program ensures safe and sanitary management of solid waste in Tennessee by regulating solid waste disposal facilities, composting facilities, transfer stations, processing facilities, convenience centers, and other solid waste-related activities throughout the state. The Solid Waste Program operates under the authority of the Solid Waste Disposal Act (<span class="icon-link-ext"></span><a href="https://www.lexisnexis.com/hottopics/tncode/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">T.C.A. §68-211-101 et seq.</a>).</p>
<p>If you are an applicant or if you live in an area where a landfill or solid waste facility is being proposed or modified, you may find information on the project in the <span class="icon-link-ext"></span><a title="Link to Dataviewer" href="https://dataviewers.tdec.tn.gov/dataviewers/f?p&#61;19035:34001::::::" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Dataviewer</a> or on our <span class="icon-link-ext"></span><a title="Link to Public Participation Opportunities" href="/content/tn/environment/ppo/waste.html">Public Participation Opportunities</a> page. To search for information in the Dataviewer, select the “Permit” tab. Additional instructions for refining your search are found at the top of the Dataviewer page.</p>

    
    

</div>


    
    
    <div class="tn-rte">
    
        <h2>Permits, Registrations, and Approvals</h2>
<p><a title="Link " href="/content/tn/environment/permits/waste/landfill-permit.html"><span class="icon-link-ext"></span>Landfill Permits</a></p>
<p><a title="Link to Landfill Permit Modifications" href="/content/tn/environment/permits/waste/permit-modifications.html"><span class="icon-link-ext"></span>Landfill Permit Modifications</a></p>
<p><a title="Link to Solid Waste Management Permit-By-Rule" href="/content/tn/environment/permits/waste/solid-waste-management-permit-by-rule.html"><span class="icon-link-ext"></span>Solid Waste Management Permit-By-Rule</a></p>
<p><a title="Link to Notification for Recovered Materials Processing Facilities " href="/content/tn/environment/permits/waste/rmpf.html"><span class="icon-link-ext"></span>Notification for Recovered Materials Processing Facilities </a></p>
<p><a title="Link to Special Waste Approval" href="/content/tn/environment/permits/waste/special-waste-approval.html"><span class="icon-link-ext"></span>Special Waste Approval</a></p>

    
    

</div>


    
    
    <div class="tn-horizontalrulev2 separator">
<div id="tn-horizontalrulev2-72727c3053" class="cmp-separator">
    <hr class="cmp-separator__horizontal-rule"/>
</div></div>


    
    
    <div class="tn-rte">
    
        <h2>Illegal Dumping</h2>
<p>Dumping of solid wastes without a permit is illegal under the Solid Waste Act, unless a private landowner is managing their own waste on their property. Often, illegal dumping cases go undetected unless they are reported by the public. If you see a solid waste dump, please contact your <span class="icon-link-ext"></span><a href="/content/tn/environment/contacts/field-offices.html" title="Environmental Field Offices">local Environmental Field Office</a> or your local public works or codes department if you live within an urban area.</p>
<p>Litter and roadside dumping are addressed under the TN Litter Law and should be reported to local authorities or the Tennessee Highway Patrol- litter control program.</p>

    
    

</div>


    
    
    <div class="tn-horizontalrulev2 separator">
<div id="tn-horizontalrulev2-fbac05722e" class="cmp-separator">
    <hr class="cmp-separator__horizontal-rule"/>
</div></div>


    
    
    <div class="columnctrl tn-columnctrl colctrl"><div>
    <div class="no-theme-chosen bgimg background-image-repeat" style="background-image: url();">
        <div class="tn-col-ctrl container">
            
